        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="7CyqZpYL4BO0aw3nbGov-1" value="Millimeter wave radar driver code suggestions&lt;div&gt;1. The numbers are expressed in macros so that it is clearer&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;2. Filtering algorithm is a single function or class&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;3. According to the manual, there should be only two types of data frames, one for delivery and one for reporting. The payload should not be mixed with the state.&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;in&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;4. After the complete frame is extracted, it is processed separately. According to the length field, you can know the frame boundary and whether the frame is valid.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;5. All drivers are modular, lora communication, espnow, sensor, etc., unified interface&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="50" y="1360" width="560" height="140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="7CyqZpYL4BO0aw3nbGov-5" value="model:&lt;div&gt;None - Replace the battery and power on again - Sleep directly&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;Unpiar&amp;nbsp; Unpaired mode&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;Normal normal mode&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Pair pairing mode&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Test test mode&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Config configuration mode (reserved for OTA?)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="640" y="1370" width="340" height="90" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="7CyqZpYL4BO0aw3nbGov-6" value="Indicator behavior:&lt;div&gt;Slow flashing - the number of flashes corresponds to different modes&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Always on - communicating&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Flashing fast - error&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Breathing light - not paired&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Radar Module - Extra Red LED Flashing - Low Battery&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;To be added&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="640" y="1470" width="310" height="90" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="7CyqZpYL4BO0aw3nbGov-7" value="Buzzer behavior (specific parameter combinations need to be further tested and determined):&lt;div&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;1.5m&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;No response&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;1-1.5m&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; 1hz&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;60-100cm&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;2hz&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;35 - 60cm&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;4hz&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;lt;35cm&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Changming&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Special buzzer behavior, indicating error&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp; descending sound,&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Frequency changes continuously&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Special buzzer behavior indicating successful pairing - uplink tone,&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Frequency changes continuously&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Special buzzer behavior, indicating low battery/extremely low battery, reminding the user to charge, downlink tone,&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;frequency step change&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="640" y="1570" width="360" height="150" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="7CyqZpYL4BO0aw3nbGov-18" value="Things to note:&lt;div&gt;You must enter pairing mode manually. If you find that it is not paired, just sleep directly. Otherwise the logic will be more complicated&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="640" y="1730" width="250" height="50" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="7CyqZpYL4BO0aw3nbGov-30" value="&lt;b&gt;Just in case, when the in-car module wakes up through lora, it can receive espnow data at the same time to prevent the ack packet loss of the leida module.&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="940" y="1360" width="310" height="80" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="7CyqZpYL4BO0aw3nbGov-40" value="1. Power-on/wake-up initialization work&lt;div&gt;Print device/debug information&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Hardware initialization - GPIO&amp;amp; buzzer&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Check if paired&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="100" y="1945" width="200" height="50" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="7CyqZpYL4BO0aw3nbGov-41" value="2. Identify the current mode based on button identification and sleep/wakeup reasons&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;user button&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Short press normal mode&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Long press (3s) Pair mode&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;dev button&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Short press test mode&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;- Long press config mode&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Unpair unpaired mode&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;None No key operation for pairing - direct sleep&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="100" y="1995" width="250" height="140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="7CyqZpYL4BO0aw3nbGov-42" value="3. Corresponding mode processing&lt;div&gt;Unpair mode - send reminder and go to sleep&lt;br&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Nomral Normal mode - normal primary reversing radar operation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Pair pairing mode, the modules inside and outside the car are paired and the communication mac address is recorded&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Test test mode, used for development and factory testing of hardware&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Config configuration mode, reserved for future use on demand, can be used for new versions/temporary modification of device configurations&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Read own battery level - low battery alarm&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="100" y="2155" width="430" height="90" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="7CyqZpYL4BO0aw3nbGov-43" value="In-car module programming" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="50" y="1920" width="190" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="7CyqZpYL4BO0aw3nbGov-44" value="4. Configure deep sleep and wake up, then enter sleep" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="100" y="2270" width="176" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="7CyqZpYL4BO0aw3nbGov-45" value="Unpair mode&lt;div&gt;Sound a buzzer reminder and then go to sleep&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="100" y="2320" width="180" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="7CyqZpYL4BO0aw3nbGov-46" value="Normal mode&lt;div&gt;Initialize lora hardware&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Initialize espnow hardware&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Control the lora module to send wake-up packets&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;After receiving the radar module lora ack, it starts to receive the data of the radar module through espnow. At this time, if it detects that the radar module has low power, it will alarm&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Continuously receives, interprets and displays distance via buzzer&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;At the same time, set the userbutton to interrupt GPIO. If the user presses the button during the period, the radar module will be notified to stop working and enter sleep to wait for the next wake-up.&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="100" y="2350" width="441" height="140" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="7CyqZpYL4BO0aw3nbGov-47" value="Test mode&lt;div&gt;To be added&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="100" y="2620" width="60" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="7CyqZpYL4BO0aw3nbGov-48" value="Config mode&lt;div&gt;To be added&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="64" y="2660" width="140" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="7CyqZpYL4BO0aw3nbGov-49" value="Pair pairing mode&lt;div&gt;Initialize espnow&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Send pairing requests in a loop&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;After receiving the reply from the radar module, record its mac address and update the nvs field paired&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Pairing successful&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Enter sleep and wait to wake up&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="100" y="2490" width="400" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
